<title>SOUTH AFRICA: SA Breweries appoints new deputy chairmen.</title>
<headline>SA Breweries appoints new deputy chairmen.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brewing giant South African Breweries Ltd said on Tuesday that it had appointed board members Cyril Ramaphosa and Donald Gordon as deputy chairmen.</p>
<p>They join Selwyn MacFarlane who already holds the post.</p>
<p>Ramaphosa, a union leader turned one of South Africa's top black businessmen, joined the SAB board earlier this year. He will take over the role of executive chairman when the current encumbant, Meyer Kahn, is absent.</p>
<p>Gordon, chairman of Liberty Life Group, has sat on the board since 1982.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
